<DocsLayout title="Effect-native interfaces" description="wseffect is a typed UI toolkit for building web interfaces with Effect and Foldkit.">
  <p class="eyebrow">A typed UI toolkit for Effect</p>
  <h1>Interfaces that stay true to your model.</h1>
  <p class="lede">wseffect brings the Elm architecture to Effect: explicit models, typed messages, pure updates, and accessible components you can compose from a single source of truth.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button-link primary" href="/getting-started/">Start building <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    <a class="button-link" href="/demos/">Explore interactive demos</a>
  </div>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Static-first by design.</strong> Use Astro or any host for content; render examples at build time and opt into runtime only for the interfaces that need it.</p></div>
  <h2>One architecture, from control to application</h2>
  <p>Build small controls with Foldkit, compose complete experiences with Themes and Foldkit UI, then add routing, persistence, offline support, and code generation as your application grows.</p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <article class="info-card"><h3>Get started</h3><p>Install published packages and choose a minimal or full starter.</p><a href="/getting-started/">Getting Started →</a><br /><a href="/getting-started/minimal/">Minimal starter</a> · <a href="/getting-started/app/">Full application</a></article>
