  <h2>Built around explicit state</h2>
  <pre tabindex="0"><code class="language-ts" is:raw>type Model = { count: number }
type Message = { _tag: 'Increment' } | { _tag: 'Decrement' }

const update = (model: Model, message: Message) =&gt;
  message._tag === 'Increment'
    ? { model: { ...model, count: model.count + 1 } }
    : { model: { ...model, count: model.count - 1 } }</code></pre>
  <p>Updates are ordinary typed transitions; commands and subscriptions make effects explicit. Read the <a href="/concepts/model-message-update-view/">Model–Message–Update–View guide</a> or browse the <a href="https://github.com/wsagency/wseffect">source on GitHub</a>.</p>
